 a critical safety signal within this drug community. For PGB, elevations in serum transaminases and clinical liver injury occur in a small but notable subset of patients. Similarly, valproate is historically known for rare but severe hepatotoxicity, especially in children under two years or those with metabolic disorders. Although the provided data does not explicitly detail valproate-induced liver injury, its established risk profile—combined with PGB’s documented effects—suggests that liver monitoring is a common and essential precaution across these agents. This shared risk factor may influence therapeutic choices and contraindications in patients with preexisting liver conditions [Data: Relationships (89, 7838, 7840); Entities (3003, 6460, 16896, 17365)].\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"Chlorpromazine (氯普吗嗪) contributes to somnolence, with smoking modulating its incidence\",\n            \"explanation\": \"氯普吗嗪, a phenothiazine antipsychotic, is linked to 倦睡 (somnolence) as an adverse reaction. Epidemiological data reveal that the frequency of this side effect varies significantly with smoking status: heavy smokers (≥20 cigarettes/day) report somnolence in only 3% of cases, compared to 11% in light smokers and 16% in non-smokers. This gradient suggests that smoking induces hepatic enzyme activity—likely CYP1A2—that accelerates chlorpromazine metabolism, thereby reducing systemic exposure and sedative effects. While the exact mechanism remains unconfirmed, this interaction illustrates how lifestyle factors can modulate drug tolerability and underscores the importance of considering patient habits in risk assessment [Data: Relationships (13195); Entities (6327, 17860)].\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"苯二氮卓类药 acts as a pharmacological enhancer in combination therapies\",\n            \"explanation\": \"苯二氮卓类药 (benzodiazepines) are not standalone actors in this network but serve as key interaction partners. Specifically, 丙戊